What Millennials, Gen X, and Baby Boomers Can Learn From Gen Z

A generational exchange about technology, mental health, work, identity, and the future of society

Every generation inherits a world it did not create, develops strategies to survive that world, and passes its assumptions to the next generation. But the world changes, and yesterday’s survival strategies can become tomorrow’s limitations.

Gen Z’s greatest lesson for older generations is that just because a system worked for you does not mean it is still working for everyone else.

Millennials, Generation X, and Baby Boomers possess invaluable experience, institutional knowledge, and historical perspective. Gen Z, however, has grown up amid smartphones, social media, economic uncertainty, a global pandemic, and the rapid development of artificial intelligence.

The opportunity is not to declare one generation superior. It is to create a dialogue in which each generation learns from the others.

Let’s explore what Millennials, Gen X, and Baby Boomers can learn from Gen Z.

